---
name: run-voice-evals
description: Run LiveKit voice agent eval scenarios. Use when the user asks to run evals, check eval scores, or benchmark agent behavior. Handles env vars, naming, GCS upload, and background execution.
---

Run evals from the `livekit/` directory using the package script:

```bash
cd <repo-root>/livekit
EVAL_RUNS=<n> EVAL_NAME=<name> bun run test:evals
```

## Filtering to specific scenarios

Use `--` to pass bun's `-t` (test name pattern) flag through the script:

```bash
EVAL_RUNS=3 EVAL_NAME=rescheduling bun run test:evals -- -t "rescheduling"
```

The pattern matches against scenario IDs (the first arg to `scenario.simulated()`), which are the `describe` block names.

## Key env vars

| Var | Default | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `EVAL_RUNS` | 3 | Attempts per scenario |
| `EVAL_NAME` | _(none)_ | Human label on the GCS result — always set this |
| `EVAL_FILTER` | _(none)_ | Substring filter on scenario IDs |
| `EVAL_SKIP_GCS` | _(unset)_ | Set to `1` to skip upload — only for local debugging |

**Never set `EVAL_SKIP_GCS` for a real run** — results must be uploaded.

## Running in the background

When asked to run evals without blocking (or two sets in parallel), launch each as a background shell process and log output to a temp file:

```bash
EVAL_RUNS=3 EVAL_NAME=confirmation bun run test:evals -- -t "confirmation" \
  > /tmp/eval-confirmation.log 2>&1 &

EVAL_RUNS=3 EVAL_NAME=rescheduling bun run test:evals -- -t "rescheduling" \
  > /tmp/eval-rescheduling.log 2>&1 &
```

Tell the user the log paths so they can `tail -f` if they want live output.

## Reading results

Results are uploaded to GCS after each run. To tail a running log:

```bash
tail -f /tmp/eval-confirmation.log
```

To check if a background run finished:

```bash
cat /tmp/eval-confirmation.log | grep -E "pass|fail|score"
```
